    <item>
      <title>Bitcoin&#39;s purpose</title>
      <link>http://localhost:44883/bitcoins-purpose/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 08 Jan 2026 19:03:35 +0700</pubDate>
      <author>mail@juju.casa (Casa de JuJu)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:44883/bitcoins-purpose/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Bitcoin as digital gold is a blasphemic statement.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div&#xA;  &#xA;    class=&#34;flex px-4 py-3 rounded-md shadow bg-primary-100 dark:bg-primary-900&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;  &gt;&#xA;  &lt;span&#xA;    &#xA;      class=&#34;text-primary-400 pe-3 flex items-center&#34;&#xA;    &#xA;    &gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;relative block icon&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 512 512&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M459.37 151.716c.325 4.548.325 9.097.325 13.645 0 138.72-105.583 298.558-298.558 298.558-59.452 0-114.68-17.219-161.137-47.106 8.447.974 16.568 1.299 25.34 1.299 49.055 0 94.213-16.568 130.274-44.832-46.132-.975-84.792-31.188-98.112-72.772 6.498.974 12.995 1.624 19.818 1.624 9.421 0 18.843-1.3 27.614-3.573-48.081-9.747-84.143-51.98-84.143-102.985v-1.299c13.969 7.797 30.214 12.67 47.431 13.319-28.264-18.843-46.781-51.005-46.781-87.391 0-19.492 5.197-37.36 14.294-52.954 51.655 63.675 129.3 105.258 216.365 109.807-1.624-7.797-2.599-15.918-2.599-24.04 0-57.828 46.782-104.934 104.934-104.934 30.213 0 57.502 12.67 76.67 33.137 23.715-4.548 46.456-13.32 66.599-25.34-7.798 24.366-24.366 44.833-46.132 57.827 21.117-2.273 41.584-8.122 60.426-16.243-14.292 20.791-32.161 39.308-52.628 54.253z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;span&#xA;    &#xA;      class=&#34;dark:text-neutral-300&#34;&#xA;    &#xA;    &gt;Original post available &lt;a href=&#34;https://x.com/AaronRDay/status/1816514466185679311&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bitcoin’s purpose is crystal clear. Satoshi Nakamoto&amp;rsquo;s whitepaper, &amp;ldquo;Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System,&amp;rdquo; explicitly outlines Bitcoin as digital cash. The whitepaper discusses creating a decentralized currency for everyday transactions, not a store of value like digital gold. Read the whitepaper and see for yourself.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="http://localhost:44883/bitcoins-purpose/featured-whitepaper.jpeg" />
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>The spiritual world today is missing masculinity</title>
      <link>http://localhost:44883/the-spiritual-world-today-is-missing-masculinity/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 19 Dec 2025 20:04:39 +0200</pubDate>
      <author>mail@juju.casa (Casa de JuJu)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:44883/the-spiritual-world-today-is-missing-masculinity/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div&#xA;  &#xA;    class=&#34;flex px-4 py-3 rounded-md shadow bg-primary-100 dark:bg-primary-900&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;  &gt;&#xA;  &lt;span&#xA;    &#xA;      class=&#34;text-primary-400 pe-3 flex items-center&#34;&#xA;    &#xA;    &gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;relative block icon&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 512 512&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M389.2 48h70.6L305.6 224.2 487 464H345L233.7 318.6 106.5 464H35.8L200.7 275.5 26.8 48H172.4L272.9 180.9 389.2 48zM364.4 421.8h39.1L151.1 88h-42L364.4 421.8z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;span&#xA;    &#xA;      class=&#34;dark:text-neutral-300&#34;&#xA;    &#xA;    &gt;Original post available &lt;a href=&#34;https://x.com/AlpacaAurelius/status/1907163607072465048&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The spiritual world today is missing masculinity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Traditionally, men were the spiritual anchors of their communities: shamans, sages, monks, prophets, priests. The rishis in India, the desert fathers in early Christianity, the Stoic philosophers, and indigenous medicine men. These were men who withdrew from the world not because they were weak, but because they were devoted to something higher, and from that space they brought wisdom back to the tribe. Masculinity was deeply tied to asceticism, presence, and spiritual depth.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="http://localhost:44883/the-spiritual-world-today-is-missing-masculinity/featured-masculin.jpg" />
    </item>
    
